Since all I've played up to now is older versions of vanilla and Slashem,
and have done EXTENSIVE polypiling, I can tell you the way it *used* to
work.
With tools, bless/curse status is the only thing guaranteed not to change
[tools with plusses or charges do not retain or regain them once they are
polyed into something that lacks them (similar to rings, but as opposed to
armor and weapons, which keep their plus values, or wands, which keep
their charges)], but *any* tool can become a magic marker, magic whistle,
magic flute, etc. - it's just not very likely. If you thought that unicorn
horns used to turn into magic markers more often than random, that was
probably your imagination. The only tools I never saw in a polypile are
magic lamp, unicorn horn, bear trap, and land mine. One of my favorites I
ever got was an 8-charge Orb of Charging (it started out as a leash),
which I used to boost a few rings and recharge several magic markers.
As for armor, I think you were wrong in the first place. Special armor
showed up in polypiles just as often as it showed up elsewhere in the
dungeon; I would always stack my armor by plus values, and hope to get
special armor in the "+3" pile. Lowly dented pots frequently became GoP,
HoB, and other nice items, once I had the polymorph spell memorized. You
*can't* get dragon scale that way, though I think I've seen every other
non-artifact armor (and weapon, silver or otherwise, *except* a rubber
hose, athame, worm tooth or crysknife) in the game in a polypile at one
point or another.

